Here is the foolproof method for perfect, fluffy brown rice.

The Golden Ratio
For almost every variety of brown rice (Long-grain, Short-grain, or Jasmine), use a 1:1 ratio.

1 cup brown rice

1 cup water (or chicken/vegetable broth for extra flavor)

Optional: 1/4 tsp salt and a splash of olive oil or butter.

Step-by-Step Instructions
Rinse the Rice: This is the secret to non-mushy rice. Place the rice in a fine-mesh strainer and rinse under cold water until the water runs clear. Drain well.

Combine: Add the rinsed rice, water, and any seasonings to the Instant Pot inner pot. Stir once to ensure all rice is submerged.  
Kristine's Kitchen

Pressure Cook: * Secure the lid and set the valve to Sealing.

Select Manual or Pressure Cook (High Pressure).

Set the timer for 15 minutes.

Natural Release (Crucial): Once the timer beeps, do not touch the valve. Let the pressure release naturally for 10 to 15 minutes. This allows the steam to finish softening the outer bran of the rice.

Fluff and Serve: Flip the valve to "Venting" to release any remaining steam. Open the lid and fluff the rice gently with a fork or rice paddle.  
Instant Pot

Pro Tips for Success
Avoid the "Rice" Button: Most "Rice" presets are calibrated for white rice. Stick to the Manual/Pressure Cook setting for brown rice.  
Live Simply

The 1:1 Rule: While stovetop recipes require more water because of evaporation, the Instant Pot is a sealed system. A 1:1 ratio prevents the rice from becoming gummy.

Doubling the Recipe: You can cook as much rice as you need as long as you don't pass the "1/2 Full" line in the pot. The timing remains the same whether you cook 1 cup or 4 cups.

